---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import BlogBreadcrumb from '../components/ui/BlogBreadcrumb.astro';
import { felix, organization } from '../data/felix';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const calLink = 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/application';

const allPosts = await getCollection('posts', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
const latestPosts = allPosts
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.publishDate.getTime() - a.data.publishDate.getTime())
  .slice(0, 4);

const expertise = [
  { label: 'Paraguay tax residency', href: '/blog/category/paraguay' },
  { label: 'European tax exits', href: '/blog/category/tax-residency' },
  { label: 'Crypto realisation strategy', href: '/blog/posts/paraguay-crypto-tax-residency' },
  { label: 'Portugal NHR alternatives', href: '/blog/posts/portugal-nhr-replacement-2026' },
  { label: 'Tax-residency glossary', href: '/blog/glossary' },
];

// AboutPage + Person JSON-LD — gives LLMs and search engines a canonical
// person entity to disambiguate "Felix Yanez-Bowker" against.
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Person',
      '@id': 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/blog/about#felix',
      name: felix.name,
      givenName: felix.givenName,
      familyName: felix.familyName,
      jobTitle: felix.jobTitle,
      description: felix.description,
      url: felix.url,
      image: felix.image,
      email: felix.email,
      knowsAbout: felix.knowsAbout,
      sameAs: felix.sameAs,
      worksFor: { '@id': 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/#organization' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/blog' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/blog/about' },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Felix and the Nomad Tax Help Guide Library"
  description="Felix Yanez-Bowker is the co-founder of Nomad Tax Help. He writes about tax residency, US LLCs, and how nomads can build clean, defensible cross-border setups."
  pageEntity={{ '@type': 'AboutPage', mainEntity: { '@id': 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/blog/about#felix' } }}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-[820px] mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <BlogBreadcrumb current="About" />
    <!-- Hero card: cream surface with photo + name -->
    <div class="surface-cream p-6 sm:p-10 mb-12" style="box-shadow: 0 14px 30px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-start gap-6">
        <a
          href="/blog/images/felix.png"
          data-lightbox="/blog/images/felix.png"
          data-lightbox-alt="Felix Yanez-Bowker"
          class="shrink-0 no-underline"
          aria-label="View larger photo of Felix"
        >
          <img
            src="/blog/images/felix.png"
            alt="Felix Yanez-Bowker"
            width="180"
            height="180"
            class="w-[180px] h-[180px] rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-teal-900/10 shadow-sm"
          />
        </a>
        <div>
          <h1 class="font-heading font-bold text-teal-900 text-3xl sm:text-4xl mb-2 leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.01em]">
            Hi, I'm Felix <span aria-hidden="true">👋</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="font-heading font-bold text-teal-900 text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.01em]">
            I help digital nomads work out whether Paraguay fits their lives and businesses.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Body content card: cream surface for readable prose -->
    <div class="surface-cream p-6 sm:p-10" style="box-shadow: 0 14px 30px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);">
      <div class="prose prose-shimmer-links">
        <p>
          I'm a co-founder of <a href="https://nomadtaxhelp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nomad Tax Help</a>, where we help people who earn across borders prepare for Paraguay residency, organise their company and apply for accounts they can use while travelling.
        </p>

        <p>
          I started this because I went through the same maze myself: trying to work out which residency to take, how to exit cleanly, what would actually protect me, and which advisers were worth listening to. Most of what I read was either too technical, too generic, or too obviously trying to sell me something. I spent a lot of time, a lot of money, and sat with a lot of stress when dealing with the perpetual question looming over me: "what the hell do I do with my taxes!?"
        </p>

        <p>
          Now, I'm based between Andorra, Spain, Indonesia and wherever the snow is good. I'm British, 29, and I've been location-independent for the better part of a decade. Before Nomad Tax Help I spent six years at a hedge fund, <a href="http://168trading.fund" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">168trading.fund</a>, and I still write a separate blog on geopolitics, demographics, and decentralisation called <a href="https://felixyanez.substack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer me"><em>The Curious Cat</em></a>. Tax residency for nomads sits at the intersection of a lot of the things I find genuinely interesting: how individuals navigate states, how money flows across borders, and what it actually takes to live a free life in 2026; and ultimately, how to become a <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/2708480-the-sovereign-individual" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sovereign Individual</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What NTH does</h2>

        <p>
          Our $5,950 Premium+ service coordinates Paraguay residency, US company setup and applications for overseas banking. We help you prepare the documents and plan around 4–7 days in Paraguay for the first appointments. Immigration approval and the cédula follow their own timelines. Where you live and perform your work matters when you assess how your income is taxed.
        </p>

        <p>
          You can read <a href="/services">what our team handles before, during and after your trip</a>, including the work you still do yourself. If you would like us to coordinate it, <a href={calLink}>apply for a free service consultation</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What I write about</h2>

        <p>
          Readers often ask whether to leave their old tax system before starting in Paraguay. There are two calendars to line up: your appointments in Paraguay and the filing deadlines where you have been living. Our <a href="/country-guides">country departure guides</a> help with the second. The guides below cover the choices that tend to come next.
        </p>

        <ul>
          {expertise.map((e) => (
            <li><a href={e.href}>{e.label}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <h2>Latest guides</h2>

        <ul>
          {latestPosts.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/blog/posts/${p.data.slug}`}>{p.data.title}</a>
              <span class="text-sm text-teal-900/60"> &middot; <time datetime={p.data.publishDate.toISOString()}>
                {p.data.publishDate.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}
              </time></span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <h2>Who checks the rules, and who handles my case?</h2>

        <p>
          Our team coordinates the Paraguay process. Qualified professionals handle the legal and filing work in your written scope. In the guides, we link directly to the authority behind a requirement. For example, our <a href="/blog/posts/paraguay-residency-ruc-tax-certificate">guide to residency documents</a> shows why a bank asking for a tax certificate may still need something else after you show it your cédula. For a decision about your own return or your departure year, use the guide to prepare your dates and questions for the adviser who will handle that filing.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Book a free clarity call: <a href={calLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">nomadtaxhelp.com/application</a></li>
          <li>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@nomadtaxhelp.com">hello@nomadtaxhelp.com</a></li>
          <li>Instagram: <a href="https://instagram.com/nomadtaxhelp_" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@nomadtaxhelp_</a></li>
          <li>LinkedIn: <a href={felix.sameAs[0]} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer me">linkedin.com/in/felix-yanez-bowker</a></li>
          <li>Personal blog (Substack): <a href={felix.sameAs[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer me">felixyanez.substack.com</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
